From: Lovelace's Square <noreply@lovelacesquare.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:22:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Status bar says "Assistant connected" while a control
 connection is authorised

With assistants allowed to join any window, the user should always see
when one has. The control server now counts the connections that have
sent an authorised request and are still open; while there are any, the
status bar shows "Assistant connected" in the accent colour, with a
tooltip saying what it means. As in WordCraft.

- deckcraft: control_server::start takes the counter; a connection is
  counted from its first authorised request until it closes, and the
  window repaints on each change. Refused connections never count.
- ui-egui: SlideApp::control_clients and assistant_connected(), the
  status bar item, and `controlClients` in ui.inspect.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Esdp3ZTPsHBV41yHxMJHnJ
